From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: mmio: use pinctrl backend if gpio-ranges is present

On BCMBCA SoCs pins have to be switched to the GPIO function in the pin
controller before they can be used as GPIOs. Let generic MMIO GPIO
controllers described in DT request/free their pins from the pin
controller when a "gpio-ranges" property is present.

Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpio/gpio-mmio.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpio-mmio.c
@@ -792,6 +792,9 @@
 	if (device_property_read_bool(dev, "no-output"))
 		flags |= GPIO_GENERIC_NO_OUTPUT;
 
+	if (device_property_present(dev, "gpio-ranges"))
+		flags |= GPIO_GENERIC_PINCTRL_BACKEND;
+
 	config = (struct gpio_generic_chip_config) {
 		.dev = dev,
 		.sz = sz,
